  "summary": "The South San Francisco City Council unanimously approved installing 31 Flock Safety automated license plate reader cameras along Highway 101 and I-280 to deter crime. The policy includes a 30-day data retention limit, a ban on sharing data with ICE, quarterly independent audits, and a public transparency webpage.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "data captured by the cameras would be deleted after 30 days unless part of an investigation, and the city would allow data to be shared with other law enforcement agencies only if requested for an investigation. Sharing data with U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement would be strictly barred.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "the program will undergo quarterly audits from an independent party to ensure compliance with the city's rules.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "The cameras would likely be procured from ALPR operator Flock Safety, at a yearly cost of $2,500 per cameras, or $77,500 for the whole city.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
  ],
